:: StoryTitle
WORKING / non-canon — Seal Day

:: Start
Smoke in the scriptorium. The Academy is burning, and you — junior scribe Verrin — have one armful left before the east stair goes.

On the table: a scrap with the last attested utterance; a stack of rival witness lists; the rite manual that still works when the Word does not.

[[Save the utterance scrap|Scrap]]
[[Save the witness stack|Witnesses]]
[[Save the empty-pipe manual|Manual]]

:: Scrap
The scrap is thin. One voice, dated, unsigned. You shove it under your tunic and run.

Behind you the stacks blacken. Later, someone will say the channel died with the witnesses. You kept the pipe's last known breath instead.

[[End|EndScrap]]

:: Witnesses
Names. Dates. Accusations of who heard what. Heavy. You stagger for the stair.

The utterance burns. The manual burns. The Academy will argue for a century about which name was true — and you gave them the quarrel.

[[End|EndWitnesses]]

:: Manual
Gesture, timing, silence where the Word used to sit. No theology — only what still binds.

You save the method. The voice and the names go to ash. Years later, clerks will keep a rite nobody can explain. You already know why.

[[End|EndManual]]

:: EndScrap
Sketch ends. Speculative only — nothing sticks to the bible.

:: EndWitnesses
Sketch ends. Speculative only — nothing sticks to the bible.

:: EndManual
Sketch ends. Speculative only — nothing sticks to the bible.
